On Nov 12, 12:48 pm, "hepta...@gmail.com" <hepta...@gmail.com> wrote:
> #dip a leather cloak into a potion of oil to create an oilskin cloak.

I don't think you've really thought this one through.  From a gameplay
perspective, it would significantly increase the value of the leather
jacket, which could be a balance issue.  Generation probabilities
would need to be rejiggered to compensate...  Also, it would change
armor slots (from the mail slot to the cloak slot), which would be
weird, especially if some wiseguy tried to exploit the fact that you
can dip a garment you are currently wearing.

If an oilskin cloak is something you just can't live without, you can
always wish for one (blessed and fireproof and +2, even) once you take
the castle.  Personally, there are several other kinds of cloaks I'd
rather have, even if it does mean I have to regrease them
periodically.

It *would* be nice if you could put a blessed bag of holding into an
oilskin sack as a lining and then treat it as a single combined
container, putting objects in or taking them out of both bags in one
move.  Especially if the oilskin sack would protect the BOH from
curses.


